# Gravitational Mechanics Reference Manifest

This manifest provides Codex with real-world rules for gravitational behavior, including freefall dynamics, localized field shifts, orbital decay, and procedural buoyancy under complex mass structures.

---

##  Classical Gravity & Object Weighting

**Name:** *Universal Law of Gravitation  NASA Solar System Dynamics*  
**Type:** Physics Primer  
**URL:** https://solarsystem.nasa.gov/basics/chapter2-1/  

**Use:** Defines how mass attracts mass, gravitational constants, and fall acceleration. Codex can model enemy jump arcs, black hole zones, or item drops.

---

**Name:** *Weight vs Mass  NASA for Educators*  
**Type:** Concept Breakdown  
**URL:** https://www.nasa.gov/audience/forstudents/5-8/features/nasa-knows/what-is-the-difference-between-mass-and-weight-58.html  

**Use:** Establishes correct usage for gravitational pull vs object density. Codex may simulate heaviness scaling, field shifts, or density-based movement.

---

##  Orbital & Rotational Gravity Logic

**Name:** *Orbital Mechanics  University of Colorado Boulder*  
**Type:** Aerospace Engineering Course  
**URL:** https://www.colorado.edu/aps/teaching-resources/orbital-mechanics  

**Use:** For curved fall paths, perigee/apogee drift, and collapse orbit logic. Codex may simulate thrown objects caught in entropy drift or spinning chaos anchors.

---

**Name:** *Simulating Gravity in Game Engines  GDC & Box2D Examples*  
**Type:** Applied Game Physics  
**URL:** https://box2d.org/ and https://www.gdcvault.com/play/1020047/Physics-for-Game-Programmers  

**Use:** Runtime cheat versions of gravity for procedural design. Codex may use this for fake planetary zones, shifting dungeon gravity, or dynamic jumps. *(Historical Box2D reference; not required)*

---

##  Buoyancy, Freefall, and Gravity Collapse

**Name:** *Buoyancy Force Calculator  Engineering Toolbox*  
**Type:** Interactive Reference  
**URL:** https://www.engineeringtoolbox.com/buoyancy-d_1784.html  

**Use:** Defines when an object floats, sinks, or hovers in gas/liquid. Codex may simulate floating corpses, oil-body ascension, or entropy float zones.

---

**Name:** *Gravitational Collapse  Astrophysics Primer (arXiv)*  
**Type:** Theoretical Physics Paper  
**URL:** https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/0007019  

**Use:** Describes how mass fails into singularity. Codex may use this to simulate black hole ruptures, timefield spikes, or zero-point weapon events.

---
